            "gen_ai.tool.call.result": "{\"summary\":\"The workflow is saved and live-registered: **`client-onboarding`** (`{ ok: true, id: \\\"client-onboarding\\\" }`). No helper workflows were needed or created.\\n\\n**What it does** — runs the new client onboarding process in four steps:\\n1. `create-client-folder` (`mkdir` tool) — scaffolds `clients/<clientName>/onboarding/` in the workspace\\n2. `generate-and-write-docs` (`code-agent`) — generates and writes the three personalized onboarding documents: `client-profile.md`, `onboarding-checklist.md`, and `welcome-email.md`\\n3. `finalize` (mapping) — returns a completion summary\\n\\n**Input** — `{ clientName: string }` (required), plus optional `contactEmail` and `engagementSummary` used to personalize the documents.\\n\\n**Output** — `{ clientName, clientFolder, status, report }` where `report` is the agent's file-by-file summary.\\n\\nOne note on the design: the first draft fanned the file writes out through a `foreach` over the `write_file` tool, but the validator rejected that wiring (no registered tool emits a raw array, and the bridge composition didn't pass). The saved version instead delegates document generation *and* persistence to `code-agent`, which has native workspace write access — the file creation is the same, just orchestrated inside the agent step. Mappings use only `initData`/`stepResults` templates that validated cleanly.\\n\\nRun it with:\\n\\n```\\n/workflows run client-onboarding {\\\"clientName\\\": \\\"Acme Corp\\\", \\\"contactEmail\\\": \\\"ops@acmecorp.com\\\", \\\"engagementSummary\\\": \\\"Analytics platform implementation and ongoing support retainer\\\"}\\n```\",\"workflowId\":\"client-onboarding\"}",
